---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Obsidixz Commercial"
  description="How Obsidixz Commercial handles enquiry email: what is collected, how messages travel and are stored, retention (24 months after enquiry closure) and your choices."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy Policy</p>
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="max-width:64ch;">
        Plain language, no theatre: what happens to an enquiry email you send us, how
        long we keep it, and the boundaries of what we can honestly claim.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section legal">
    <div class="wrap prose" style="max-width: 880px;">

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        Obsidixz Commercial is an unregistered business brand operated by Richard
        Oluwadunmininu Olasehinde (“we”, “us”). No claim is made here of incorporation,
        a registered office or any registration that does not exist. Privacy questions:
        <a href="mailto:obsidixz@outlook.com">obsidixz@outlook.com</a>. Commercial
        enquiries go to <a href="mailto:obsidixz.commercial@outlook.com">obsidixz.commercial@outlook.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What you give us, and when</h2>
      <p>When you email us, you choose what to share. It typically includes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your email address and, if you provide them, your name and company</li>
        <li>The content of your message — your product or research need, quantities, markets, timeframes</li>
        <li>Anything you deliberately attach — though we ask you <strong>not</strong> to send banking credentials, identity documents or confidential product designs in your initial enquiry</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We operate no enquiry form, customer account, mailing list or newsletter. This website collects nothing you type — there is nothing to type into. Page-load request data is a separate matter, handled by the host: see “Cookies, analytics and hosting” below.</p>

      <h2>How your message travels and is stored</h2>
      <p>
        You send email via your chosen email provider. It travels over the internet to
        the Commercial mailbox, a Microsoft Outlook inbox. That means:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your provider processes your message in transit and in your own sent folder, under its terms and privacy policy — outside our control.</li>
        <li>Microsoft processes the message to deliver, store and serve the Commercial mailbox, under Microsoft’s terms and privacy policy — outside our control, and not something we can switch off.</li>
        <li><strong>Your provider’s role and Microsoft’s role do not remove our responsibilities.</strong> As the operator of the Commercial mailbox we remain responsible for what happens to what reaches us — reading it, using it for the purpose you wrote in, storing it and deleting it as described below — whatever infrastructure either of your providers runs.</li>
        <li>We access the mailbox to read and respond. We do not operate separate enquiry databases, CRMs or automated processing pipelines for it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we use your information for</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Assessing whether and how we can help, and responding to you</li>
        <li>Preparing feasibility views, scopes and quotations if you ask for them</li>
        <li>Keeping the working record of an enquiry so we can honour follow-ups</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>No automatic forwarding.</strong> Your enquiry is never automatically
        forwarded to suppliers or any third party. If contacting a supplier ever becomes
        appropriate, it is assessed separately with you first, and agreed in writing.
        We do not sell your information, build marketing lists from it, or use it for
        advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Our retention policy: 24 months after an enquiry is closed.</strong> We
        review inactive enquiries after <strong>12 months</strong> to decide whether to
        close and, later, delete them. Closure means the conversation has concluded —
        typically when a project is delivered or the enquiry is declined or goes quiet.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is our retention policy — a decision we have made, not a technical description of the mailbox or of Microsoft’s infrastructure. Deleting a message from the mailbox removes our working copy of it; it cannot recall your own sent copy, other people’s copies of the same thread, or provider-side copies and backups that neither you nor we control. If you ask us to delete something and part of it cannot be deleted — for example, an accepted quotation kept for record-keeping — we will say so plainly.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies, analytics and hosting</h2>
      <p>
        This website sets <strong>no cookies</strong> and uses <strong>no analytics,
        advertising or tracking services</strong>, because none are configured. The site
        is hosted on <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> (static hosting for this repository’s
        published build). As the host, GitHub’s systems process ordinary request data —
        for example IP address, browser or user-agent string and the requested URL, with
        timestamps — under GitHub’s own privacy statement. We do not use those host logs
        to profile you, and they are not combined with your enquiry by us. If the hosting
        arrangement ever changes, this notice will be updated at that cutover rather than
        naming a provider some day in the future without knowing whether the site sits
        there.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        You may email <a href="mailto:obsidixz@outlook.com">obsidixz@outlook.com</a> to
        ask what information we hold about you, ask for a correction, or request deletion.
        Where deletion is constrained by provider behaviour or by legitimate record-keeping
        needs — for example, an agreed quotation you accepted — we will tell you plainly
        rather than pretend otherwise.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also simply choose not to send an enquiry; nothing on this site requires
        it. If you correspond with us, ordinary email confidentiality applies — email is
        not a secure channel, so please keep sensitive detail out of it.
      </p>

      <h2>Security — honestly stated</h2>
      <p>
        The Commercial mailbox is a personal Microsoft Outlook mailbox. Email is not a
        confidential channel — whatever provider carries it, and whatever safeguards apply,
        it passes through systems we do not fully control, and we do not describe it as
        secure. Access to the mailbox is limited to the responsible individual.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Please never send banking credentials or payment-card details by email —
        now or later, by any channel we might suggest.</strong> If a project genuinely
        requires material you would treat as confidential (for example, unreleased product
        specifications), that is a separate matter we assess and agree in writing before
        anything is sent — it is not a blanket invitation to email identity documents or
        credentials.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If how we handle enquiries changes — for example, if a CRM or ticketing tool is
        introduced — this page will be updated and the date below refreshed. Material
        changes affecting open enquiries will be flagged to the people involved.
      </p>

      <p class="updated">
        Last updated: 9 November 2026 · Contact the responsible individual via
        <a href="mailto:obsidixz@outlook.com">obsidixz@outlook.com</a>.
        See also: <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
